  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 933 PM CDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nThe long term period will largely be influenced by an upper level\nridge and subsequent sfc high pressure system looming over the Deep\nSouth and slowly shifting eastward into the lower Mississippi Valley.\nA few features to watch will be how remnants of Tropical Storm Bertha\ninteract with a cold front south of our area. How these two features\ninteract will largely dominate the forecast for Friday into Sunday.\nWe currently have low to medium rainfall chances through that time\nperiod and are outlooked for a Marginal risk (level 1 of 4) for flash\nflooding from the Weather Prediction Center. If the front shifts over\nthe area and stalls, the flooding threat will increase. However,\nthere is still too much uncertainty to dive into details as it is\nseveral days out. If you have outdoor plans early this weekend, it's\nhighly encouraged to check back in for updates. Otherwise, as the\naforementioned ridge shifts eastward, dry weather should return to\nthe area early next week along with a warming pattern as highs begin\nto climb back into the mid to upper 90s. Additional heat products\nwill likely need to be considered if trends continue.",
